    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, our lineup construction prioritizes aggressive matchups against high-xERA arms, anchored by **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** (74.26), **Luis Arraez** (69.53), and **Dylan Beavers** (69.52). **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** remains our most reliable asset, benefiting from a soft 4.91 xERA matchup against Nick Martinez; despite a slight park penalty, his elite skill set and prime spot in the order make him an easy start. **Luis Arraez** and **Dylan Beavers** are both primed to exploit a favorable wind condition and a weak matchup against Ryan Johnson and Bryce Elder, respectively. **Jonathan Aranda** (64.35) and **Jeremiah Jackson** (64.53) also stand out as high-upside plays; **Jeremiah Jackson** specifically gains a massive 16% boost from his venue, which offsets his lower lineup positioning and makes him a primary engine for our category targets today.\n\nThe most difficult decision on our bench involves **Bryce Harper**, who sits at 55.05\u2014falling just short of the 60+ threshold required to displace our current starters. While **Bryce Harper** maintains a strong xwOBA, his score was suppressed by an unfavorable matchup against Ryan Weathers (3.46 xERA) and the conservative Optimizer output that prioritizes the platoon advantages held by players like **Taylor Ward** and **Jung Hoo Lee**. Our strategy remains disciplined: we are prioritizing the aggregate daily efficiency score to maximize output across all five categories.\n\nManagers should monitor the status of **Cal Raleigh** and **Yainer Diaz** closely, as both are currently hovering in the 48-point range due to tough matchups against Nathan Eovaldi and Sean Burke. With several other players, including **Geraldo Perdomo**, **Drew Gilbert**, **Daulton Varsho**, and **Kyle Karros**, sitting in that high-40s to mid-50s \"marginal\" tier, the lack of confirmed lineups remains our primary risk. Should any of these players move down in the order, we will be forced to reconsider their start status to protect our daily game caps. We are keeping a close eye on **Lawrence Butler** and **Braden Montgomery** on the bench as potential pivots if we receive word of late-inning rest or lineup shifts for our starters.",
